    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d827">

                <pb facs="1116" n="1102" xml:id="pg1102"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/15268: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Kunming</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Ringwalt</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Kunming</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-02-18T11:00:00+07:00">February 18,
                            1944—11 a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received February 18—8:27 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>10. Yunnan–Kweichow Pacification Headquarters has forwarded to Consulate General
                    through the special delegate a report on the Milo incident (telegram No. 6,
                    January 12, 5 p.m.<anchor n="13" xml:id="d827-f1"/>). Although not entirely
                    satisfactory, headquarters Y force agrees with this office that provided Embassy
                    concurs no useful purpose would be served in making further representations.
                    Despatch follows.<anchor n="14" xml:id="d827-f2"/>
                </p>
                <p>Sent to Chungking, repeated to Department.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Ringwalt</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
